<!-- Signing -->
<section class="sec" id="signing"><div class="wrap"><div class="tr-single">
  <div class="sec-head"><p class="q">Who signs what?</p><h2 class="h2">Each side signs on their own phone.</h2><p class="lede" data-new="1">Sarah signs when she writes the record. David signs when he confirms it, on his own phone. A record is sealed only when everyone it names has signed, so everyone is on the same page. If they disagree, both versions are kept: Sawaza is a witness, not a judge.</p><p class="lede" data-new="1">Every record keeps its history: who wrote it, who answered it and when, and every change is shown.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<!-- Nobody can change it, no money -->
<section class="sec deep" id="change"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="sec-head"><p class="q">What stays true?</p><h2 class="h2" data-new="1">A signed record can't change quietly. Nobody touches your money.</h2><p class="lede" data-new="1">Sawaza never holds or moves money. It keeps the record of it.</p></div>
  <div class="tr-cc">
    <div class="tr-col yes">
      <p class="lbl" data-new="1">You can</p>
      <ul>
        <li data-new="1">Remove your own copy, never the other side's.</li>
        <li data-new="1">File it your own way: its item, its space, its account.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="tr-col no">
      <p class="lbl" data-new="1">What stays true</p>
      <ul>
        <li data-new="1">A record is sealed once it is signed, so any change shows.</li>
        <li data-new="1">The other side's copy stays theirs.</li>
